# ============================================
# Line endings
# ============================================
# .editorconfig mandates `end_of_line = lf`, but that only tells the *editor*.
# Without this file, a contributor with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default)
# checks text files out as CRLF and commits them as LF, so every line of every
# file they touch shows up as changed on the next checkout. `eol=lf` makes the
# working-tree form agree with the .editorconfig contract on every platform.
#
# NOT YET APPLIED TO THE EXISTING TREE. Creating this file does not retroactively
# fix files that are already committed with CRLF in the index; that needs
#     git add --renormalize .
# which stages the whole repository and must be its own reviewed commit. Until
# then, the first pass through a given file can still show whole-file churn.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated by `dotnet new gitignore`, the EF Core tools and the SqlClient
# driver: they are written with CRLF on Windows and must not be normalised.
*.sln.DotSettings.user text eol=crlf
*.dbmdl text eol=crlf
*.jfm text eol=crlf
*.publishsettings text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.slnx text eol=lf

# Windows scripts are genuinely more readable with CRLF, and PowerShell and cmd
# both accept either, so the churn tradeoff is settled in their favour.
# (Everything else - .cs, .cshtml, .csproj, .json, .yml, .md, .props, .targets -
#  keeps the repo-wide `eol=lf` from the rule above.)

# ============================================
# Binary assets
# ============================================
# Extension list produced from `git ls-files`. Tracked binary files today:
#   src/NewVixSmart.Web/wwwroot/favicon.ico
#   src/NewVixSmart.Web/wwwroot/lib/bootstrap-icons/fonts/bootstrap-icons.woff
#   src/NewVixSmart.Web/wwwroot/lib/bootstrap-icons/fonts/bootstrap-icons.woff2
#   src/NewVixSmart.Web/wwwroot/lib/fonts/cairo/cairo-{arabic,latin,latin-ext}.woff2
# `text=auto` alone would let Git sniff these as text and corrupt them.
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.eot binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.bmp binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.7z binary

# Database files must never be treated as text either: a .bak is a full copy of
# the production database, and both .gitignore and .dockerignore keep it out of
# the tree, but `binary` is the belt to that suspenders.
*.bak binary
*.trn binary
*.mdf binary
*.ndf binary
*.ldf binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite3 binary

*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pdb binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.wasm binary
